---
pagination:
  data: collections.postTypes
  size: 1
  alias: group
  addAllPagesToCollections: false
permalink: "/{{ group.segment }}/"
layout: layouts/pagealign.liquid
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ group.segment | capitalize }}"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
eleventyImport:
  collections: ["post"]
---
{%- comment %} One index per post type, at the same URL segment its posts live
   under, so /notes/ lists what /notes/<slug>/ contains. Posts themselves are at
   /<segment>/<slug>/, so an index at /<segment>/ cannot collide with them.
   /archive/ still lists every type together; this is the filtered view.
{% endcomment -%}
<ol class="posts h-feed">
{%- for post in group.posts %}
  {%- comment %} socialHtml and postTypeIconHtml must be captured HERE, before
     the `page: post` override below — see post-list-entry.liquid's header
     comment and post-type-icon.liquid's. {% endcomment -%}
  {%- capture socialHtml %}{% include "partials/post-social-counts.liquid", post: post %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- capture postTypeIconHtml %}{% include "partials/post-type-icon.liquid", post: post %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- include "partials/post-list-entry.liquid", post: post, page: post, socialHtml: socialHtml, postTypeIconHtml: postTypeIconHtml -%}
{%- endfor %}
</ol>
